            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0570" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12534: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-23T10:00:00+08:00">November 23, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 23—12:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>870. Following telegram has been received from Vice Consul at Foochow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 22, 5 p.m. New government formally established this morning
                            when the members took oath. Highest authority of the new government
                            invested in a central committee of 11 members, 6 of whom are Nineteenth
                            Route Army adherents. Under this committee are 3 departments and 2
                            ministries. The departments are Culture, Defense, and Economics; headed
                            by Chen Ming-shu, Li Chai-sum, and Chiang Kuang-nai, respectively.
                            Eugene Chen is Minister for Foreign Affairs. The Finance Minister has
                            not yet been appointed. The country is known as the Chinese People’s
                            Republic and the government as the Chinese People’s Revolutionary
                            Government. Li <pb facs="0571" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/> Chai-sum is
                            concurrently President of the People’s Republic and Chiang Kuang-nai is
                            concurrently Governor of Fukien.</p>
                        <p>The new national flag was displayed over all government buildings today;
                            also throughout the city by order of the police.</p>
                        <p>The new government is opposed oy practically all classes of Fukienese
                            here and has been set up by compulsion.</p>
                        <p>Friction is reported to have already broken out between the militarists
                            and politicians over control. Foochow quiet.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
